cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this result, please cite the tagged release.
title: "Two theta prime races in one fixed window"
abstract: "For the 547/727 and 571/599 prime races, a weighted average of at most two common doublings gives any pair of normalised moves in the square from −5.85 to 5.85 in each coordinate. After every real starting height H ≥ 1, all targets fit before CH for one finite constant C. The existence proof is unconditional."
